dbSta: crossing_cones, crossing_signatures and crossing_strip

Tcl commands for timing only the register-to-register paths of a flat
design that are not contained in one macro (a macro is an instance
name's first level), in pieces that fit memory:

crossing_signatures: the sets of macros the paths run through, found by
propagating each net's macro masks forward from the registers in one
pass, without enumerating a path.

crossing_cones: the design cut to the logic those paths can touch for a
set of macros: the nets between two macros, the logic forward and
backward to the first register, the side inputs' fan-in, every load of
a kept net and the clock network into every kept register. Optionally
makes the registers only side inputs reach false path starts, and a
path group through the crossing nets.

crossing_strip: route guides, special wiring, blockages and
obstructions removed, for a design timed from SPEF.

Carried by bazel-orfs for //tools/carve; not upstreamed. Retires on a
//:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it.
